As many have probably noticed we've got a temporary git tree set up at
git://github.com/connectivity/bluez.git as long as kernel.org isn't
functional. My original intent was to send "applied" mail notifications
only once we've merged back to kernel.org, but since this has taken much
longer than expected I'm going to start sending these mails anyway now.

So there's going to be a temporary flood of emails, but it will help
me and hopefully also the patch writers to better track what has been
applied.

